ligned}{\\theta }_{R} & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{(-3)}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the ray lies in the second quadrant. So, we find the angle in the second quadrant that has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polar equation of the ray is \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980294/state.json" "file_sha256" "7573a241f0f104e940ddce4d0579fd4fa7f67cc52e49589d7bd65b1ad94ba99b"} {"question" "q-321889" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980294/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8245313d6a1a9363cc6b5889ea8e012c290586419323a4fbba4aa5e1cfd1f2de"} {"question" "q-321889" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980294/state.json" "file_sha256" "7573a241f0f104e940ddce4d0579fd4fa7f67cc52e49589d7bd65b1ad94ba99b"} {"question" "q-321889" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\pi}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980294/state.json" "file_sha256" "7573a241f0f104e940ddce4d0579fd4fa7f67cc52e49589d7bd65b1ad94ba99b"} {"question" "q-120701" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980294/assets/410822e9d39446151be39bc8402